### Phase 4: Weekly/Phase Progression

**Objective**: Show how the plan evolves over time based on adaptation principles.
```
{
  "program_duration_weeks": 3,
  
  "phase_progression": [
    {
      "phase_name": "Week 1 - Adaptation",
      "goals": [
        "Establish baseline performance on all exercises",
        "Adapt to caloric deficit",
        "Master exercise technique"
      ],
      "training_adjustments": {
        "uses_template": "weekly_schedule_template",
        "specific_notes": "Start conservative on weights - focus on form and establishing working weights for progression"
      },
      "nutrition_adjustments": {
        "uses_template": "training_day_meals + rest_day_meals",
        "specific_notes": "Full caloric target; monitor hunger, energy, performance"
      },
      "expected_outcomes": "May lose 1-2 lbs, mostly water weight; strength should maintain",
      "progress_tracking": [
        "Weigh daily, take weekly average",
        "Track all working set weights/reps",
        "Rate energy 1-10 daily",
        "Rate hunger 1-10 daily"
      ]
    },
    
    {
      "phase_name": "Week 2 - Progression",
      "goals": [
        "Begin progressive overload on exercises",
        "Continue deficit adherence",
        "Assess recovery and adjust if needed"
      ],
      "training_adjustments": {
        "uses_template": "weekly_schedule_template",
        "specific_notes": "Apply progression rules: add reps or weight to all exercises where possible"
      },
      "nutrition_adjustments": {
        "uses_template": "training_day_meals + rest_day_meals",
        "specific_notes": "If energy drops significantly, add 100 calories on hardest training days"
      },
      "expected_outcomes": "Lose 0.5-1 lb; strength should maintain or slightly increase on some lifts",
      "progress_tracking": "Continue week 1 metrics + take progress photos"
    },
    
    {
      "phase_name": "Week 3 - Peak & Assess",
      "goals": [
        "Push performance while managing fatigue",
        "Assess total fat loss and body composition",
        "Plan next phase if continuing"
      ],
      "training_adjustments": {
        "uses_template": "weekly_schedule_template",
        "specific_notes": "Continue progression where possible; don't force progression if recovery is suffering"
      },
      "nutrition_adjustments": {
        "uses_template": "training_day_meals + rest_day_meals",
        "specific_notes": "Consider refeed on day 5 if feeling depleted (add 300 carb calories)"
      },
      "expected_outcomes": "Lose 0.5-1 lb; cumulative loss 2-3 lbs fat; strength maintained on most lifts",
      "progress_tracking": "Final weigh-in, photos, measurements; strength test on key lifts",
      "reassessment": "Compare actual outcomes to predicted; adjust plan for next phase"
    }
  ]
}

Phase 5: Practical Guidance & Troubleshooting
Objective: Equip the user with knowledge to handle real-world challenges.
{
  "adherence_strategies": {
    "challenge": "Consistency",
    "research_backed_solutions": [
      {
        "strategy": "Implementation intentions",
        "description": "Pre-decide when and where you'll train (e.g., 'Monday 6am at home gym')",
        "research": "Increases follow-through by 30% (Gollwitzer, 1999)"
      },
      {
        "strategy": "Habit stacking",
        "description": "Attach workout to existing habit (e.g., 'After morning coffee, I work out')",
        "research": "Leverages existing neural pathways for consistency (Clear, 2018)"
      },
      {
        "strategy": "Meal template adherence",
        "description": "Use same meals to reduce decision fatigue",
        "research": "Reduces cognitive load, improves adherence (Baumeister et al., 2018)"
      }
    ]
  },
  
  "troubleshooting": [
    {
      "problem": "Not losing weight after week 1",
      "possible_causes": [
        "Underestimating food intake",
        "Overestimating activity",
        "Water retention masking fat loss",
        "Metabolic adaptation (unlikely in week 1)"
      ],
      "solutions": [
        "Weigh/measure all food for 3 days to verify intake",
        "Wait another week - fat loss isn't linear",
        "If confirmed plateau after 2 weeks, reduce calories by 100-150/day"
      ],
      "research_note": "Weight fluctuates 2-4 lbs daily due to water, food volume, hormones - focus on weekly averages"
    },
    
    {
      "problem": "Excessive hunger or low energy",
      "possible_causes": [
        "Deficit too aggressive",
        "Inadequate protein or fat",
        "Poor sleep",
        "High stress"
      ],
      "solutions": [
        "Increase calories by 100-200 (prioritize protein/fat)",
        "Shift meal timing to when hunger is worst",
        "Prioritize 8+ hours sleep",
